# The EFFECT this patch must have, as extended regexes over the file it touches
# (Libraries/LibRequests/Request.cpp). Checked only when the patch's exact bytes
# are NOT in the tree, so upstream's own fix -- or any equivalent one -- is
# recognised as "already fixed" instead of being reported as missing, which is
# what happened to Ulf on a tree NEWER than our pin.
#
# The effect: the branch that decides the body is fully delivered (the one that
# calls the user's finish callback) must ALSO tear the request down, so the
# callbacks holding GC::Roots are dropped and the response fd is closed.
#
# The window matters. defer_teardown() already appears in stop() and
# did_transfer(), so a whole-file grep for it passes on a tree WITHOUT the fix --
# verified, and pinned by a test. So anchor on the branch condition and require
# the call within the following few lines.
@window 12 has_received_all_reported_bytes =
user_finish_called = true
defer_teardown\(\);
